# Secrets never live here — they live in %LOCALAPPDATA%\hermes\.env and are
# forwarded into the container by terminal.docker_forward_env.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Run state: watermarks, probe results, scraped snapshots, logs. All machine-
# and moment-specific — a probe run from this laptop says nothing about what a
# VPS would see, and committing one invites someone to read it as a fact.
#
# The whole directory is ignored rather than a list of extensions: enumerating
# them already let state/health.err and state/origin-comparison.md slip into a
# commit, and the next new extension would slip too.
#
# `state/*` not `state/`: git will not re-include a path whose parent directory
# is excluded, so the .gitkeep negation below silently does nothing with the
# directory form — and a fresh clone then has no state/ for digest.mjs to write
# its watermark into.
state/*
!state/.gitkeep

# Evaluation runs are generated. The labelled SET is committed (it is derived
# from the client's files and is the test); individual run outputs are not.
eval/before.json
eval/after.json
eval/run-*.json
eval/run-*.log
eval/*.report.md

# Generated from criteria/relevance.md by eval/make-holdout.mjs. Committing it
# would let the two drift apart silently, and the derived copy is worthless if
# it no longer matches its source.
criteria/relevance.holdout.md

# Node, if a dependency ever becomes necessary. Currently the harness is
# deliberately dependency-free — plain fetch on Node 22.
node_modules/

# OS noise
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
